    <h1>Description of Proposed Project</h1>
    <p>
        My auntie owns a clothes hiring business, and I would like to create a website for her. 
        She has struggled to create her own, as template websites such as Shopify make it difficult 
        to hire out products. Furthermore, many potential customers are often confused by having to 
        contact her business directly through Instagram. By creating a website, it would not only 
        reduce her workload but also increase her business’ outreach to customers.
    </p>

    <p>The website will contain many key elements:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Landing page</li>
        <li>Product display featuring an option to book try-ons</li>
        <li>Contact section including email, Facebook, Instagram, and other social media</li>
        <li>
            Detailed product pages:
            <ul>
                <li>Available sizes and colours</li>
                <li>Description of the item</li>
                <li>Suggested occasions</li>
                <li>Customer reviews</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>A page dedicated to positive reviews</li>
        <li>Pop-ups for current sales or promotions</li>
        <li>General business location information</li>
        <li>
            About Us page:
            <ul>
                <li>The story of how the company was created</li>
                <li>Its mission: affordable hiring, helping people feel special, and reducing clothing waste</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
            Booking system:
            <ul>
                <li>Customers can book multiple clothing items</li>
                <li>A timetable showing available dates</li>
                <li>Optional email reminders 24 hours before booking</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
            Booking confirmation:
            <ul>
                <li>Terms and conditions provided</li>
                <li>Email sent to confirm booking details</li>
                <li>Instructions on clothing care and returns</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
    </ul>
